		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=17875#p17875"><![CDATA[
Hi Everyone,<br><br>I am proud to announce the release of our first game for the iPhone, iPad and iPod Touch platforms, iShuffleGame. This is an implementation of a deck shuffleboard game in which users launch their discs using the accelerometer to create realistic game play. Visit iShuffleGame.com or look for us on iTunes for more information. <br><br>We used the bullet-2.75 library as the core physics engine, which gave the game smooth, realistic physics with minimal effort. <br><br>I would like to thank all of the developers and members of these forums for helping this game come to life.<br><br>Sincerely,<br>DB<br>President,<br>Tatami Software, Inc.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6025">TatamiSoftware</a> — Mon Mar 15, 2010 7:25 pm</p><hr />
